<title>COLOMBIA: Ecopetrol sets force majeure on crude shipments.</title>
<headline>Ecopetrol sets force majeure on crude shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's state-run oil company Ecopetrol declared force majeure Monday on two crude shipments totaling 750,000 barrels until the country's main oil pipeline could be repaired after a leftist rebel attack, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said it was &quot;impossible&quot; to say when the shipments, due to be dispatched to the United States over the weekend, could be loaded.</p>
</text>
